<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls on Portugal 10-yr bond at auction.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Portugal 10-yr bond at auction.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Mangement auction of 25 billion escudos of 10-year fixed rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>ISSUES: Republic of Portugal</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE:  July 8, 1997</p>
<p>MATURITY: 23 February 2007</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: 22.89 bln esc</p>
<p>COUPON:6.625 pct</p>
<p>AVG ACC YIELD: 6.426011 (pvs 6.5594)</p>
<p>HIHEST ACCPT:  6.44 pct</p>
<p>LOWEST 6.37 pct</p>
<p>BIDS: 63.34 bln esc</p>
<p>PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Annual</p>
<p>S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 164.97</p>
<p>billion escudos the total amount of bonds issued.</p>
</text>
